---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate disclosure — OpsPrimer"
  description="How OpsPrimer earns money and what that means for what you read here."
>
  <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>

  <p><em>Last updated: 14 August 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    Some of the links on this site are affiliate links. If you click one and buy
    a subscription, I may receive a commission from the company — at
    <strong>no extra cost to you</strong>. You never pay more for using my link,
    and the price you see is the price you'd get going direct.
  </p>

  <h2>Who I currently have affiliate relationships with</h2>

  {/* ⚠️ MANTENHA ATUALIZADO. Adicione cada programa no dia em que for aprovado
      e remova no dia em que sair. Lista desatualizada e o mesmo defeito que o
      dossie documenta no post japones (ShareASale, arquivo 05). */}

  <p>
    <strong>None, at the moment.</strong> Every outbound link on this site is a
    plain link and earns me nothing. If that changes, this list is where you'll
    see it — updated the day a programme is approved, not later.
  </p>

  <p>
    So the disclosure at the top is written for how this site is meant to work,
    not for how it currently earns. Right now it earns nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>What this does not change</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>I only write about tools I have used myself.</li>
    <li>
      I state a real weakness for every tool I cover — including the ones that
      pay me.
    </li>
    <li>
      Where a product I earn nothing from is the better fit, I say so and link
      it without an affiliate tag.
    </li>
    <li>
      No company reviews, approves, edits or pays for these articles before
      publication.
    </li>
    <li>
      I don't accept payment for placement, and I don't publish sponsored posts.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to avoid the affiliate link entirely</h2>
  <p>
    If you'd rather I didn't earn anything, just type the company's name into
    your browser and go direct. Nothing on this site is gated behind an
    affiliate link.
  </p>

  <p>
    This disclosure is made in accordance with the U.S. Federal Trade
    Commission's 16 CFR Part 255, "Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and
    Testimonials in Advertising".
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:michelthedev@gmail.com">michelthedev@gmail.com</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
